# 6. Common decision system of several experiments

For channels

\[
\kappa_1,\ldots,\kappa_P
\]

define

\[
\boxed{
C_k^\cap
=
\bigcap_{p=1}^P
\mathcal R_k(\kappa_p).
}
\]

Then

\[
C^\cap=(C_k^\cap)_k
\]

is the exact greatest coherent decision system available from every channel separately.

Operational meaning:

\[
A\in C_k^\cap
\]

iff the same \(k\)-action stochastic decision channel can be implemented from every \(\kappa_p\), possibly using a different post-processing for each experiment.

This object exists even when the Blackwell meet does not.

