# 9. New research direction: decision-arity filtration

The hierarchy

\[
\mathcal R_2(\kappa),
\mathcal R_3(\kappa),
\ldots
\]

contains progressively stronger operational information.

Blackwell's k-decision orders satisfy a strict hierarchy in general.

This suggests an independent invariant:

\[
\boxed{
a(\kappa,\mu)
=
\min\{
k:
\mathcal R_k(\mu)\not\subseteq\mathcal R_k(\kappa)
\},
}
\]

with \(a=\infty\) for Blackwell domination.

Interpretation:

> the minimum number of actions needed for a decision problem to witness that \(\kappa\) fails to dominate \(\mu\).

This "decision arity" is not the same as output alphabet size.

It measures the operational complexity of an informativeness distinction.

Dedicated prior-art search required.

