# 10. New research direction: representability defect by arity

For a completed common system \(C^\cap\), define an arity-k realization defect relative to genuine channels, for a declared compact-set metric \(d_H\), by

\[
\eta_k(C^\cap)
=
\inf_\mu
d_H(
\mathcal R_k(\mu),
C_k^\cap
).
\]

A full weighted defect could be

\[
\eta(C^\cap)
=
\inf_\mu
\sup_{k\ge2}
w_k
d_H(
\mathcal R_k(\mu),
C_k^\cap
).
\]

This is not yet canonically normalized.

Torgersen's exact deficiency-as-sup-distance result strongly suggests that the correct full metric should be defined through normalized decision/risk functionals rather than an arbitrary Hausdorff metric.

Research target:

\[
\boxed{
\text{completion projection distance}
\stackrel{?}{=}
\text{Le Cam deficiency distance to genuine experiments}.
}
\]

