# 11. Historical correction: Le Cam already built much of the needed ambient world

Torgersen's account records that:

- generalized variables repair ordinary-test nonclosure under pointwise limits;
- generalized decision rules/transitions repair inadequacy of ordinary Markov kernels;
- abstract experiments are families of nonnegative normalized vectors in L-spaces;
- deficiency distance equals a natural sup-distance on experiment functionals;
- standard/conical measures convert experiment statements into measure statements;
- for finite parameter sets, information order becomes dilation order;
- local comparison of differentiable experiments produces a local deficiency and local information order;
- for the linear normal models studied there, that local order is Fisher-information order.

Therefore the Cold War Renaissance result here is not "invent generalized experiments."

The useful new candidate is the explicit complete-lattice **coherent decision-system completion** and its representability interface with Le Cam's generalized-experiment machinery.

The collision audit must determine whether this exact object already appears under another name.

